 ## Overview
-Triplane and Planar Representations encode 3D scenes using a set of learnable 2D feature grids (planes) aligned with the canonical coordinate axes, rather than a 3D voxel grid [G]. This approach reduces memory complexity from cubic to linear relative to resolution while maintaining high fidelity [G]. It distinguishes itself from standard 3D voxel grids by leveraging 2D convolutions for efficient feature aggregation and from pure MLPs by avoiding local minima issues associated with high-resolution spatial queries [13901-eg3d-triplane-representation.md]. It serves as a generative backbone for state-of-the-art 3D-aware GANs and efficient neural rendering of dynamic or outdoor scenes [13901-eg3d-triplane-representation.md][18169-image-conditional-triplanar-representation.md].
+Triplane and Planar Representations encode 3D scenes using a set of learnable 2D feature grids (planes) aligned with the canonical coordinate axes, rather than a 3D voxel grid [G]. This approach reduces memory complexity from cubic to linear relative to resolution while maintaining high fidelity [G]. It distinguishes itself from standard 3D voxel grids by leveraging 2D convolutions for efficient feature aggregation and is specifically optimized for integration into Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) for 3D-aware image synthesis [S2]. It serves as a generative backbone for state-of-the-art 3D-aware GANs and efficient neural rendering of dynamic or outdoor scenes [S2][18169-image-conditional-triplanar-representation.md].
 
